dialect grammar
grammar stdio.jpg.snapshot
extension jpg
start document
comment none

# P2-FG2: real M1-dialect grammar, replacing the pre-Phase-2 ABNF-flavored placeholder (wrong
# header dialect -- `dialect protocol stdio.jpg.snapshot` on one line, `%x` ranges, `/`
# alternation, `~` negation -- none of it this dialect's real syntax, see
# `📖️grammar-recipe.md` §1.1). `📸️jpg` is BINARY-NATIVE (per the ticket's own classification for
# this wave): the TEXT DSL wire form `store::ArtifactDsl::parse_dsl`/`print_dsl` actually round
# trip (`../../🦀️.rs`) is a semio preamble line, then the real JFIF byte stream
# (SOI..EOI, ITU-T T.81/ISO 10918-1) hex-encoded verbatim -- so this grammar honestly models the
# TEXT form (a hex-dump grammar, matching png's own accurate precedent per the recipe) and does
# NOT re-describe the binary marker-segment structure that job belongs to
# `../💾️binary/📡️.protocol.semio`.
#
# `comment none`: hex digits are lowercase-only and never contain `#`; kept for consistency with
# every other stdio artifact's snapshot grammar and so a stray `#` in future fixture growth fails
# loudly as a real parse mismatch instead of silently vanishing as a comment.
document = artifact-mark payload
artifact-mark = "stdio.jpg"
payload = hex*
